patrone-guest-tools (0.1.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * First release: Hyper-V's integration services and VirtualBox's guest
    utilities, each only under its own hypervisor (the user, 2026-10-28:
    "hyper-v and virtualbox support just like a windows guest os would
    have"). Hyper-V's file copy runs again (Ubuntu's unit waits for a
    device Linux 6.10 dropped), its daemons run from any installed
    kernel's tools (the live session boots the disc's kernel), and chrony
    takes the Hyper-V host's clock as a source. VBoxClient starts in
    Wayland sessions, and every account may use VirtualBox's shared
    folders; the VirtualBox packages (multiverse) are dependencies, since
    apt left virtualbox-guest-x11 out as a recommendation.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:00:00 -0500
